    "answer": {
      "short": "$9.3\\ \\text{m s}^{-1}$",
      "worked": "Take the window as the origin, with upward positive.\n$$x=Vt,\\qquad y=-5t^2.$$\nLet $y=-6.2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-5t^2&=-6.2\\\\t&=\\sqrt{\\frac{6.2}{5}}\\ \\text{s}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $t=\\sqrt{\\frac{6.2}{5}}$ and $x=10.4$ into $x(t)=Vt$:\n$$\\begin{align*}10.4&=V\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{6.2}{5}}\\right)\\\\V&=\\frac{10.4}{\\sqrt{6.2/5}}\\\\V&\\approx9.3\\ \\text{m s}^{-1}\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
